   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "הָיָה חוֹפֵר בּוֹר, שִׁיחַ וּמְעָרָה – קוֹצֵץ וְיוֹרֵד וְהָעֵצִים שֶׁלּוֹ (וְכוּ׳). בְּעָא מִינֵּיהּ יַעֲקֹב הַדְיָיבָא מֵרַב חִסְדָּא: עֵצִים שֶׁל מִי?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that if «he was digging a cistern, a ditch, or a cave, he may cut downward and the wood is his.» The Sage «Ya’akov of Hadeyyav raised a dilemma before Rav Ḥisda: To whom does the wood belong?» The mishna says that the wood is his, without specifying to which of the two individuals this refers, the owner of the tree or the owner of the land."
  }
